From: Claude <claude@anthropic.local>
Date: Wed, 19 Aug 2026 00:02:30 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] docs+infra: local MinIO setup for developing against the S3
 storage backend

- docker-compose.yml: MinIO + a one-shot mc container that creates the
  oms-uploads bucket the backend expects. Opt-in -- STORAGE_BACKEND still
  defaults to local disk, no Docker required for normal dev.
- .env.example: uncomment-and-go MinIO quickstart block (endpoint,
  region, minioadmin/minioadmin credentials matching the compose file)
- README: new 'Optional: local S3-compatible storage (MinIO)' section
  under Backend Setup with the docker compose up flow, console URL, and
  how to reset/switch back to local disk

S3StorageBackend verified end-to-end against a live S3-compatible HTTP
server (save/exists/read_bytes/download_to/presigned_url/delete all
round-tripped correctly), and the full /files route test suite (upload,
download, list, scoping) passes unmodified with STORAGE_BACKEND=s3
pointed at that server -- confirms the real request path works, not just
the storage module in isolation. Docker/MinIO itself isn't available in
this environment, so final verification against actual MinIO should be
done locally, but the protocol-level behavior this compose file wires up
is now proven.
